In the /bin/sh file used to exec nethack, the existence of a $PAGER
environment variable is checked.

It is assumed the $PAGER is a single word; in my case, however,
PAGER is set to 'less -sm'.  This causes the sh 'test -x' to scream.

A partial solution is enclosing every appearance of $PAGER in double
quotes.   But when $PATH is searched for $PAGER, the search will fail
and $PAGER will be unset.  I don't know how you can extract the 'less'
from 'less -sm' to solve that.  Any ideas?

-- Ran
